.TH "GF-ADMIN-USERS-ADMIN-LOGOUT-USER" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-admin-users-admin-logout-user - Logouts user revokes all auth tokens devices for the user user of issued auth tokens devices will no longer be logged in and will be required to authenticate again upon next activity


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf admin-users admin-logout-user [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Logouts user revokes all auth tokens devices for the user user of issued auth tokens devices will no longer be logged in and will be required to authenticate again upon next activity

.PP
If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled, you need to have a permission with action \fBusers.logout\fR and scope \fBglobal.users:*\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for admin-logout-user

.PP
\fB--user-id\fP=0
	UserID


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	Organization ID (env: GF_ORG_ID)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgf-admin-users(1)\fP
